            <div xml:id="d691">

                <pb facs="0622" n="616" sameAs="frus:frus1939v04/pg616"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.8227/5: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Walton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-05-29T14:00:00-00:44">May 29, 1939—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received May 29—12:55 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>37. Department’s telegram No. 16, May 2, 4 p.m. Liberian Government agrees to
                    article III but suggests that article be omitted from <pb facs="0623" n="617"
                        xml:id="pg617"/> text of the agreement and that article be ratified by an
                    exchange of notes. Question of favored nation clause raised.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Walton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
